# Runs tests/test_detect_stub.py -- and ONLY that test -- inside
# surgvu26-train.sif, WITHOUT pandas/matplotlib/seaborn installed. requests,
# PIL and tqdm are left REAL (the base image already ships them -- see
# below), not stubbed.
#
# THE DECISION THIS INFORMS (controller ruling R22, blocking --yolo from
# shipping; scope corrected by rulings R34 then R35, a stub-construction
# bug fixed by R37): no internet on Grand
# Challenge means no runtime pip install in the submission image. The staged
# yolov5's models/common.py and its own import chain (utils/dataloaders.py,
# utils/general.py, utils/plots.py) hard-import pandas, requests, PIL, tqdm,
# matplotlib and seaborn at module scope, and DetectMultiBackend (the class
# Detector._load loads through) lives in models/common.py. None of the six
# is actually CALLED on the detection path for a .pt checkpoint (see
# tests/test_detect_stub.py's docstring for the full per-name trace).
#
# R22 scoped this experiment to three of those six (pandas, requests, PIL).
# R34 corrected the SCOPE to all six -- and that six-name version's own
# up-front guard assertion (built for exactly this purpose) fired on its
# first outing: requests, PIL and tqdm turned out to be genuinely
# importable in surgvu26-train.sif, because it shares its base image
# (pytorch/pytorch:2.5.1-cuda12.1-cudnn9-runtime) with
# containers/surgvu26-submission.def and containers/Dockerfile, and that
# base already ships all three. R35 corrected the scope again, in the other
# direction: the submission image's genuinely MISSING set, as inferred from
# the shared base plus the submission .def's own additions (only
# opencv-python-headless and PyYAML -- confirmed by reading all three
# container files directly), is pandas/matplotlib/seaborn. THIS is the
# experiment that scope settled on: stub only those three, let
# requests/PIL/tqdm resolve against the real, installed packages, exactly
# as the actual submission container would.
#
# THIS JOB is the empirical half of the argument, now correctly scoped.
# condor/detect_smoke.sub (existing, unmodified) proves the detector works
# when the real packages ARE installed; this job proves -- or disproves --
# that it still works when pandas/matplotlib/seaborn are genuinely ABSENT
# and only sys.modules stubs stand in for them, while requests/PIL/tqdm stay
# real. condor/detect_stub.sh installs nothing but pytest -- it does NOT
# install pandas/matplotlib/seaborn (they must stay genuinely absent) and
# relies on the base image for requests/PIL/tqdm. tests/test_detect_stub.py
# itself asserts, before doing anything else, BOTH directions: that
# pandas/matplotlib/seaborn are genuinely NOT importable here, AND that
# requests/PIL/tqdm ARE -- if either assumption is wrong, the experiment
# proves nothing (or proves something that would not transfer to the real
# submission image) and the relevant assertion fails loudly, by name,
# rather than let a false or misleading pass through. This two-sided guard
# is what caught the R34 -> R35 correction in the first place; it stays.
#
# R37: this job ran once at this scope (cluster 9686702) and got past
# models.common's own import chain, then hit torch itself --
# torch._dynamo.trace_rules enumerates module specs at import time and
# ValueErrors when a sys.modules entry's __spec__ is None, which a bare
# stub module's is by default. tests/test_detect_stub.py's stub class now
# gives every stub (and every submodule stub) a real ModuleSpec; nothing
# about what gets stubbed, what stays real, or this job's dependency
# footprint changed.
#
# THIS EXPERIMENT VERIFIES: whether pandas/matplotlib/seaborn can be
# sys.modules-stubbed without perturbing anything Detector.detect actually
# needs, in an environment shaped like "pytorch/pytorch base + real
# requests/PIL/tqdm + no pandas/matplotlib/seaborn". IT DOES NOT VERIFY:
# that the actual built surgvu26-submission.sif has exactly that package
# set -- the inference rests on all three container definitions declaring
# the same base and the submission .def adding nothing beyond
# opencv-python-headless/PyYAML; if that image was ever built from a
# different base tag, or had packages added/removed outside what its .def
# shows, this experiment's environment would no longer match the real one
# and this job's guard cannot detect that divergence (it can only detect a
# divergence between ITS OWN environment, surgvu26-train.sif, and the
# assumption).
#
# Run from the repo root, after:
#   mkdir -p logs
#   condor_submit condor/detect_stub.sub

universe                = container
container_image         = file:///staging/n/nkalthoff/surgvu26/surgvu26-train.sif

executable              = condor/detect_stub.sh

# Required for two independent reasons: reaching the .sif under
# /staging/n/nkalthoff (same as every other container_image=file:///staging/...
# job in this repo), and reaching best.pt / the yolov5 checkout / the sample
# clip under /staging/groups/bhaskar_opscribe, which the test reads by
# absolute path rather than via transfer_input_files (HTCondor refuses to
# transfer files directly out of /staging -- see condor/extract.sub).
+WantStagingMount       = true

should_transfer_files   = YES
when_to_transfer_output = ON_EXIT
# pyproject.toml is intentionally not transferred, same reasoning as
# condor/detect_smoke.sub: conftest.py puts `src` on sys.path itself.
#
# config/ and scripts/ are NOT needed here, same reasoning as
# condor/detect_smoke.sub: tests/test_detect_stub.py imports only
# surgvu.detect and surgvu.perceive, and neither reads a config/ file at
# import time.
transfer_input_files    = src, tests, conftest.py

# CPU-only: DetectMultiBackend loads fine on cpu (Detector defaults to
# device="cpu") and this is a smoke test, not a throughput benchmark.
request_cpus            = 2
request_memory          = 8GB
# Smaller than detect_smoke.sub's 4GB: this job's whole point is that it does
# NOT pip-install pandas/matplotlib/seaborn (only pytest, see
# condor/detect_stub.sh) -- requests/PIL/tqdm come from the base image, not
# a pip install here -- so there is no transitive-wheel headroom to reserve
# for. best.pt (14 MB) and the yolov5 checkout are read in place from
# staging, not transferred.
# The surgvu26-train.sif image is 2.97GB and must land on the execute node's
# disk before anything runs, so 2GB cannot even hold it: cluster 9686697 was
# HELD with "disk usage exceeded request_disk" at 3,128,612 KB used against
# 2,097,152 KB requested, having received 3.19GB. Sized with headroom for the
# image plus the scratch pip install. Second instance of the R33 failure mode.
request_disk            = 8GB
transfer_output_files   =

log                     = logs/detect_stub_$(Cluster).log
error                   = logs/detect_stub_$(Cluster).err
output                  = logs/detect_stub_$(Cluster).out

queue 1
